| Decision | Options | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|
| Fonts | (a) keep Google Sans and install it from the user's own copy; (b) switch the tokens to fonts with open licences that are packaged (for example Google Sans Flex, if its licence allows packaging, or Roboto Flex / Inter), shipping or depending on them | (b): a one-command install cannot depend on fonts it may not redistribute; verify each font's licence and Arch availability first |
| Config discovery | candidate A or B (§2) | follow the Task 11 (runtime spike) probe |
| Login screen | greetd + tuigreet; SDDM; our own Quickshell greeter later | greetd + tuigreet for the first release |
| Distribution channel | AUR `mat-shell-git` only; later an AUR release package; later Arch `extra` | AUR `-git` first, release package once versioned |
| Installer hosting | raw GitHub URL; a short domain | decide when the repository is public |
